  "authoring_method": "Case inputs and expected semantics (support references, conflicts, primary flags, certainty rows, and rejections) were hand-authored from the frozen contract and independently reviewed. Source-result digests, the fusion-policy hash, conflict identifiers, and per-case canonical digests were then bound mechanically with the frozen byte algorithms over the hand-authored inputs. Expected outputs were not generated by the implementation under test.",
  "semantics_notes": [
    "A candidate is `conflicting` when any P2T4ConflictV1 row references it, including LOW_CONFIDENCE_EVIDENCE; conflicting candidates are never primary and use NOT_APPLICABLE_CONFLICTING with null certainty.",
    "Low-confidence classification uses the original source confidence with strict `<` against the policy floor before any adjustment; null confidence is never below the floor.",
    "Primary selection ranks each (kind, normalized claim, structural refs) group by conflict eligibility, positive support, original confidence descending with null last, then observation_id ascending; only the top non-conflicting member is primary and adjustment happens afterwards.",
    "Terminal precedence is identity/version -> strict validation -> admissibility -> correlation -> typed status -> fusion; each stage inspects ASR before Vision and the first rejection is terminal.",
    "The BOTH correlation rejection reports expected_identity=NONE, observed_identity=UNKNOWN, observed_status=null, and field_code=CORRELATION_ID.",
    "Policy `match_view_version` is the frozen literal `vision_policy_match_view-v2`; T4 applies the existing vision-policy-match-view-v2 recipe once per segment/candidate text and adds no Vision-side rejection.",
    "Themes are Vision-only: no narration matching, no primary flag, no uncertainty row; a finite theme confidence below the floor emits LOW_CONFIDENCE_EVIDENCE with a null narration reference.",
    "`transcript_raw` is never a matching source; it binds provenance only through the ASR source-result digest and never appears in any output."
  ],
